      ],
      "source": "https://www.sedgwickcolorado.com/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Sedgwick grew along the United Pacific Railroad in the early 1900s, turning the town into a bustling rail hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.uncovercolorado.com/towns/sedgwick/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Just a short drive north, Jumbo Reservoir offers hunters and anglers a chance to fish warm‑water species and camp by the lake.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.sedgwickcolorado.com/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Sedgwick sits in a semi‑arid climate zone, marked on maps as BSk under the Köppen system.",
